n/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/widget-layout/commits/c37a3ccdf0648cfa5be3a1e97ef9cd4976bf8830/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-23T17:54:29Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-23T17:54:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"e2e test pipeline fixes (#298)\n\n* chore: fix e2e tests\n\n* fix: adopt standard login logic\n\n* fix: increase timeouts for slow SSO in CI\n\n* fix: debugging\n\n* fix: use proxy URL instead of direct console.stage.redhat.com\n\nIn CI, tests were connecting directly to console.stage.redhat.com\ninstead of going through the proxy at stage.foo.redhat.com:1337.\nThis caused tests to fail because the insights-qa user doesn''t have\naccess to widget-layout features on the production console.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove HCC_ENV_URL from baseURL configuration\n- Use PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL or default to stage.foo.redhat.com:1337\n- Add debug logging to track URLs and page state\n\nThe proxy routes /widget-layout* to the local app, so tests will\nnow properly test the local build instead of production.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: add hostAliases to resolve stage.foo.redhat.com in CI\n\nAdd hostAliases configuration to the run-e2e-tests task to make\nstage.foo.redhat.com resolve to localhost (127.0.0.1 and ::1).\n\nThis allows the Playwright tests to connect to the proxy sidecar\nat https://stage.foo.redhat.com:1337, which routes /widget-layout*\nto the local app and everything else to console.stage.redhat.com.\n\nMatches the pattern used in other repos like frontend-starter-app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: run tests sequentially with React initialization wait\n\nChanges:\n- Add 3s wait after SSO login for React app to initialize\n- Increase test timeout from 120s to 180s for slow SSO\n- Disable fullyParallel to prevent race conditions\n- Force workers: 1 to ensure sequential test execution\n\nTests were failing intermittently because:\n1. React app hadn''t fully rendered before checking for buttons\n2. Parallel execution caused resource contention in CI\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove debug logging and deduplicate TrustArc blocking\n\nCleanup changes:\n- Remove all debug console.log statements from test-utils.ts\n- Remove disableCookiePrompt() function (redundant with base.ts)\n- Delete unused helpers/login.ts file\n\nTrustArc blocking is already handled globally in base.ts at the\ncontext level, so the page-level blocking was unnecessary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8eefa4d3cfb4bf265a3eec6a587aff9d313831a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/widget-layout/git/trees/8eefa4d3cfb4bf265a3eec6a587aff9d313831a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RedHatInsights/widget-layout/git/commits/c37a3ccdf0648cfa5be3a1e97ef9cd4976bf8830","verification":{"payload":"tree 8eefa4d3cfb4bf265a3eec6a587aff9d313831a2\nparent b15c9201dc8f880c7346f20c84069f1a6bf76da8\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1774288469 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774288469 +0100\n\ne2e test pipeline fixes (#298)\n\n* chore: fix e2e tests\n\n* fix: adopt standard login logic\n\n* fix: increase timeouts for slow SSO in CI\n\n* fix: debugging\n\n* fix: use proxy URL instead of direct console.stage.redhat.com\n\nIn CI, tests were connecting directly to console.stage.redhat.com\ninstead of going through the proxy at stage.foo.redhat.com:1337.\nThis caused tests to fail because the insights-qa user doesn''t have\naccess to widget-layout features on the production console.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove HCC_ENV_URL from baseURL configuration\n- Use PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL or default to stage.foo.redhat.com:1337\n- Add debug logging to track URLs and page state\n\nThe proxy routes /widget-layout* to the local app, so tests will\nnow properly test the local build instead of production.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: add hostAliases to resolve stage.foo.redhat.com in CI\n\nAdd hostAliases configuration to the run-e2e-tests task to make\nstage.foo.redhat.com resolve to localhost (127.0.0.1 and ::1).\n\nThis allows the Playwright tests to connect to the proxy sidecar\nat https://stage.foo.redhat.com:1337, which routes /widget-layout*\nto the local app and everything else to console.stage.redhat.com.\n\nMatches the pattern used in other repos like frontend-starter-app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: run tests sequentially with React initialization wait\n\nChanges:\n- Add 3s wait after SSO login for React app to initialize\n- Increase test timeout from 120s to 180s for slow SSO\n- Disable fullyParallel to prevent race conditions\n- Force workers: 1 to ensure sequential test execution\n\nTests were failing intermittently because:\n1. React app hadn''t fully rendered before checking for buttons\n2. Parallel execution caused resource contention in CI\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove debug logging and deduplicate TrustArc blocking\n\nCleanup changes:\n- Remove all debug console.log statements from test-utils.ts\n- Remove disableCookiePrompt() function (redundant with base.ts)\n- Delete unused helpers/login.ts file\n\nTrustArc blocking is already handled globally in base.ts at the\ncontext level, so the page-level blocking was unnecessary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwX5VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAArcQAChg0JUaa9EwJkzAjG//C6IX\nJ95s/rr0kVEjiI+OM/I/TBqGzl0a3Y8aHKr/rtU9k3VunQR96cwjcuuScrbv3B/O\n4uVwXY1XTM+CC5o0JnL12zLGXRGc6z8BTU/2Ks9WeD9blak/bxJWuu45P+phkjNl\nE0VNNjtKgydZYjG07JoGDRfSmBEL8P1opoTo0FEGEGsoJ+eQPhkYJa7qVRdvMJ9Y\n+UhDq9EEYin+biR+/3JUJKYFNFY2+LJYH6a12pL3nJXtIE0Q5YM066rbYzepfVoW\nwTmmkHdLN4N+bz5MEb2HHqI0zITJgal6MuUR+TTUnKDLMl/QcxIJn1kVN/F83nbV\nJkxV0OFJS786oPsrM0tf+62sPNNJOAQT0Ys3wOa3c49qvTcER76bsgx9Y/QTU1zs\nAAvDeUKBj7tmJi2YSD1O1yZpNI0JP/LpZ/VlI6rck7muVSHf34xTmSp4nfssMJ7e\nmq5IwdBfdp32nvVbM2RdP5L7ymJzP6A/HkgLX9QXl92f1JjH7Z+Cv8D0c4+1ufSH\nGZoKzT8Y/2NmlvnFYkUoxqHW+5qxQNsLPDuliL954QNDt50zLuSH9Ih23uDuIwZJ\nek4/gHgrPMfJ048MIOveLUUytY6kOSpwa1KTU5hyAC28XLiKQ6gEVxnNELfDfSX5\nEsJ3h7S8Q4yMWtxQN8Fl\n=zC7E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-23T17:54:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/r