":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/e92d797980451f5a50343e5a0b5acfb3330f44c2","node_id":"C_kwDOLcPQu9oAKGU5MmQ3OTc5ODA0NTFmNWE1MDM0M2U1YTBiNWFjZmIzMzMwZjQ0YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96","sha":"696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96"}],"sha":"e92d797980451f5a50343e5a0b5acfb3330f44c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/e92d797980451f5a50343e5a0b5acfb3330f44c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65102852?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuapare","id":65102852,"login":"joshuapare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTAyODUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-23T03:52:23Z","email":"65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-23T03:52:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: remove immer from watch event batching (#49)\n\n* fix: remove immer from watch event batching to fix Wails class instance errors\n\nWails v3 bindings return class instances (e.g. ListResult) which Immer\ncannot draft, causing \"produce can only be called on draftable things\"\nerrors on every watch event flush. Replace produce() with manual\nimmutable updates (shallow array copy + spread) in useEventBatcher and\nuseWatchState. This also removes Immer''s proxy wrapping and deep-freeze\noverhead on the hot path.\n\n* fix: update totalResources in watch state updater\n\ntotalResources was inherited from the old state via spread, so it became\nstale when a new resource key arrived via a watch event. This affected\npolling decisions, isFullySynced, and syncProgress.","tree":{"sha":"377259bccb09d4462f944762db578a04ce4e1bcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/377259bccb09d4462f944762db578a04ce4e1bcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96","verification":{"payload":"tree 377259bccb09d4462f944762db578a04ce4e1bcb\nparent dd6cd05332e721e1efce631e878f0c545909e00b\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1774237943 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774237943 -0500\n\nfix: remove immer from watch event batching (#49)\n\n* fix: remove immer from watch event batching to fix Wails class instance errors\n\nWails v3 bindings return class instances (e.g. ListResult) which Immer\ncannot draft, causing \"produce can only be called on draftable things\"\nerrors on every watch event flush. Replace produce() with manual\nimmutable updates (shallow array copy + spread) in useEventBatcher and\nuseWatchState. This also removes Immer''s proxy wrapping and deep-freeze\noverhead on the hot path.\n\n* fix: update totalResources in watch state updater\n\ntotalResources was inherited from the old state via spread, so it became\nstale when a new resource key arrived via a watch event. This affected\npolling decisions, isFullySynced, and syncProgress.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwLj3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAASgQAERu1NNJ+AG9AnF6aEqmUU2j\npC3Xa5tY47REs9VtBHdXLgOFcHXvIhTkjQ0Us5o8Yb5DSDBr7gmm998hKqZTyWyr\n9XgCEeIIRR428T+hAyXPqD9GQ5KKIremUuEgIJLMrgyqEVJaWs9tnjWgQuYGry5h\n9LJ+kMh0ZhsdWEIB0mpUYFBothIfa9v1Aiee0VUwRZugQdZ8ApZ0SHWPh9bT7qVR\n14wzbbCVU24b9GHEyZOFZbdZ86OnR8KiCrNKrnOcsAOUveHIAsTXC7c1J3lv02WJ\n7prmGaj3TuJk9CC2rz0XsKwZGtO3a8GMlzUZ1lVoiBWxUKDgHac9kpDbiQnam0s8\nGnwCIGPkEO2WfzkMkj1TegjTcdDHeoL8+2Bq4mxsgYujHyj/LVhwwavLumT7RKgW\n8GP2FRg6VpUyubycVPZzsixIbt9X47/U15pefg9tFXTuY3YnAbmh1x/PsuXKGp9m\ntmizx20nLkaABXI+ZoXRygqRp3gTm3VG7gmgJEDsA8aGfiwIMS7OZHsA+iq7UlyT\nzwSTVnw6dw24RApIpTZ5zAlwO3JQhOkV96cXzpTRMJTxltLvBVTTaUbPuQZzzois\nfWvJtS13CupQPqbMI4qC0b2MN6scY1y9ktIopilVr71/aMNP9Ip0jZt0nMDR64uy\nHBUm/EmfI3Oo4EKUb5x4\n=F3iI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-23T03:52:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96","node_id":"C_kwDOLcPQu9oAKDY5NmVjMzgzZmM4N2YxMDhhMWM2OTFmOTI1NjJmNGMyMjUxZDFmOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/dd6cd05332e721e1efce631e878f0c545909e00b","sha":"dd6cd05332e721e1efce631e878f0c545909e00b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/dd6cd05332e721e1efce631e878f0c545909e00b"}],"sha":"696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/696ec383fc87f108a1c691f92562f4c2251d1f96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65102852?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuapare","id":65102852,"login":"joshuapare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTAyODUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/dd6cd05332e721e1efce631e878f0c545909e00b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T15:12:23Z","email":"65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T15:12:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: terminal input and cleanup (#47)\n\n* fix: base64-encode terminal input before WriteSession\n\nWails v3 serializes []byte parameters as base64 over JSON. The frontend\nwas sending raw keystrokes which failed with \"illegal base64 data\".\n\n* chore: reduce terminal debug log noise\n\n- Remove raw ANSI buffer dump, log buffer size instead\n- Remove per-keystroke \"got input\" log from exec mux\n- Remove \"past lock\" breadcrumb log\n- Log session count instead of full session objects in ListSessions\n- Log only command and tty in StartSession instead of full opts/context\n\n* fix: centralize signal handling, remove dead code, fix ListSessions lock\n\n- Centralize host-process signal forwarding into a single Manager-level\n  goroutine instead of one per terminal session. Prevents signal delivery\n  contention with multiple terminals open.\n- Use RLock instead of Lock in ListSessions (read-only operation).\n- Remove unused cleanPTYOutput function and listenOnOut function.\n\n* fix: eliminate terminalManager race and cascade shutdown to sessions\n\n- Move terminal.NewManager() from runLocalMux goroutine into\n  ServiceStartup so c.terminalManager is initialized before any\n  goroutine can access it.\n- Derive session contexts from m.ctx instead of context.Background()\n  so manager shutdown cascades to all active PTY sessions.","tree":{"sha":"1f9f813f960abaa7a19e5c24670f522070405343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/1f9f813f960abaa7a19e5c24670f522070405343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/dd6cd05332e721e1efce631e878f0c545909e00b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f9f813f960abaa7a19e5c24670f522070405343\nparent 3ccb6414502d0891a57be8f5ecc902e3b400fd28\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1774192343 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774192343 -0500\n\nfix: terminal input and cleanup (#47)\n\n* fix: base64-encode terminal input before WriteSession\n\nWails v3 serializes []byte parameters as base64 over JSON. The frontend\nwas sending raw keystrokes which failed with \"illegal base64 data\".\n\n* chore: reduce terminal debug log noise\n\n- Remove raw ANSI buffer dump, log buffer size instead\n- Remove per-keystroke \"got input\" log from exec mux\n- Remove \"past lock\" breadcrumb log\n- Log session count instead of full session objects in ListSessions\n- Log only command and tty in StartSession instead of full opts/context\n\n* fix: centralize signal handling, remove dead code, fix ListSessions lock\n\n- Centralize host-process signal forwarding into a single Manager-level\n  goroutine instead of one per terminal session. Prevents signal delivery\n  contention with multiple terminals open.\n- Use RLock instead of Lock in ListSessions (read-only operation).\n- Remove unused cleanPTYOutput function and listenOnOut function.\n\n* fix: eliminate terminalManager race and cascade shutdown to sessions\n\n- Move terminal.NewManager() from runLocalMux goroutine into\n  ServiceStartup so c.terminalManager is initialized before any\n  goroutine can access it.\n- Derive session contexts from m.ctx instead of context.Background()\n  so manager shutdown cascades to all active PTY sessions.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwAbXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7W0QAB6T5c6gfmKPeRoPfzNLsaJ5\nlXDBJFtEsO6vC2fFe9Q/4rG2fYbV7Kn1VFW21Bx1luVKjlGKfU4vo7+n37ZuzxlI\nd7HScUX4fzl5AsWza+3ikRhuNbACUbo3tFNXIv14v0ncfNkREi2rzCZNQeY/j71Y\ncOPj4mO