are/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuapare","id":65102852,"login":"joshuapare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTAyODUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/e9db9b7612b8894343352e24f5229e200f8e52c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-18T04:08:06Z","email":"65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-18T04:08:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: recovery path after failed plugin reconnection (#40)\n\n* fix: show recovery-failed state and retry button after plugin crash\n\nWhen a plugin exhausts its crash recovery budget, connections previously\nwent silent with no UI feedback. Now the frontend listens for\nplugin/crash_recovery_failed and plugin/recovered events, surfaces a\n\"Plugin crashed — recovery failed\" status in the connection footer, and\noffers a \"Retry Plugin\" button that reloads the plugin with a fresh\ncrash budget.\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review feedback\n\n- Critical: Move budget reset out of ReloadPlugin into dedicated\n  RetryFailedPlugin method so automated crash recovery doesn''t\n  inadvertently clear the crash budget\n- Minor: Add try/catch to retryPlugin so failed state is restored\n  immediately if ReloadPlugin throws\n- Trivial: Remove non-null assertions after guard checks\n- Trivial: Show both failed and error counts in footer label\n- Trivial: Log errors instead of silently swallowing in catch handlers\n- Regenerate Wails bindings for new RetryFailedPlugin method","tree":{"sha":"608daa634f44be865d8a60f2b3a5744fcddc8ff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/608daa634f44be865d8a60f2b3a5744fcddc8ff3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/e9db9b7612b8894343352e24f5229e200f8e52c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 608daa634f44be865d8a60f2b3a5744fcddc8ff3\nparent 476249743e6c2ada60c5dd05d9f9a34a13961417\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1773806886 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773806886 -0500\n\nfix: recovery path after failed plugin reconnection (#40)\n\n* fix: show recovery-failed state and retry button after plugin crash\n\nWhen a plugin exhausts its crash recovery budget, connections previously\nwent silent with no UI feedback. Now the frontend listens for\nplugin/crash_recovery_failed and plugin/recovered events, surfaces a\n\"Plugin crashed — recovery failed\" status in the connection footer, and\noffers a \"Retry Plugin\" button that reloads the plugin with a fresh\ncrash budget.\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review feedback\n\n- Critical: Move budget reset out of ReloadPlugin into dedicated\n  RetryFailedPlugin method so automated crash recovery doesn''t\n  inadvertently clear the crash budget\n- Minor: Add try/catch to retryPlugin so failed state is restored\n  immediately if ReloadPlugin throws\n- Trivial: Remove non-null assertions after guard checks\n- Trivial: Show both failed and error counts in footer label\n- Trivial: Log errors instead of silently swallowing in catch handlers\n- Regenerate Wails bindings for new RetryFailedPlugin method","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpuiUmCRC1aQ7