com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/2c7a95a04d48911f208883e24dedc52fe60a3e33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T03:00:06Z","email":"joshuabpare@gmail.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T03:00:06Z","email":"joshuabpare@gmail.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"message":"fix: Windows build — use logging.Logger in terminal manager, share testLogger helper\n\nThe Windows-specific terminal manager still referenced *zap.SugaredLogger\nafter the non-Windows variant was updated to the SDK logging interface.\nAlso extracted testLogger into a shared helpers_test.go so plugin tests\ncompile on all platforms.","tree":{"sha":"caa885c65c139e611e1144ca73d7fdf5a6de5ee0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/caa885c65c139e611e1144ca73d7fdf5a6de5ee0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/2c7a95a04d48911f208883e24dedc52fe60a3e33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65102852?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuapare","id":65102852,"login":"joshuapare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTAyODUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/2c7a95a04d48911f208883e24dedc52fe60a3e33","node_id":"C_kwDOLcPQu9oAKDJjN2E5NWEwNGQ0ODkxMWYyMDg4ODNlMjRkZWRjNTJmZTYwYTNlMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/14e64a7c5a14227c5760417d0d3255ca78a616d2","sha":"14e64a7c5a14227c5760417d0d3255ca78a616d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/14e64a7c5a14227c5760417d0d3255ca78a616d2"}],"sha":"2c7a95a04d48911f208883e24dedc52fe60a3e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/2c7a95a04d48911f208883e24dedc52fe60a3e33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65102852?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuapare","id":65102852,"login":"joshuapare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTAyODUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/14e64a7c5a14227c5760417d0d3255ca78a616d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T02:22:57Z","email":"65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T02:22:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resource): add Resource Graph Engine (#29)\n\n* feat(resource): add ref-counted string interner for graph edge dedup\n\n* feat(resource): add ResourceEntry, RegistryStore interface, and MemoryStore implementation\n\n* feat(resource): add ResourceIndexer interface and async dispatcher\n\n* feat(resource): add RelationshipGraph with bidirectional edge management\n\nIntroduces GraphNode, GraphEdge, DependencyTree types and RelationshipGraph\nwith forward/reverse maps, dedup, selector cache, declaration registry, and\nconnection-scoped removal that preserves cross-connection edges.\n\n* feat(resource): add graph query APIs (GetRelated, GetRelationshipChain, GetDependencyTree)\n\n* feat(resource): add GraphIndexer for edge extraction from declarations\n\n* feat(resource): restructure sink to update registry/indexers unconditionally\n\n* feat(resource): wire registry, dispatcher, and graph into controller\n\n* feat(resource): add GraphService for Wails-bound graph queries\n\nIntroduces GraphService wrapping RelationshipGraph with GetRelated,\nGetRelationshipChain, and GetDependencyTree query methods. Adds Graph()\naccessor to Controller interface and concrete implementation.\n\n* test(resource): add end-to-end integration tests for registry→graph pipeline\n\n* fix(resource): address review findings from graph engine implementation\n\n- Populate Labels/UID/CreatedAt from watch metadata in sink entries\n  (fixes broken label-selector relationship resolution)\n- Prevent observeResponse from overwriting existing registry metadata\n- Return slice copies from EdgesFrom/EdgesTo to avoid data races\n- Add Dispatcher.Flush() barrier for deterministic test synchronization\n- Guard Dispatcher.Enqueue against sends after Stop\n- Improve RemoveEdgesForConnection comment clarity\n\n* chore: bump plugin-sdk to v0.3.1\n\n* fix(resource): address remaining review findings for PR #29\n\n- Fix TOCTOU race in dispatcher Enqueue/Flush with stopping channel\n- Clone labels maps in sink and memory store to prevent shared-map mutation\n- Use composite declMapKey for declarations to prevent cross-plugin overwrites\n- Validate direction input in GraphService instead of defaulting\n- Add cross-connection check in CheckLabelSelectorsForEntry\n- Add Shutdown method to controller for clean dispatcher teardown\n- Rename misleading interner test names\n- Document Key() separator invariant\n\n* fix(resource): second round of review fixes for PR #29\n\n- Add 30s timeout context for bootstrap RPCs in OnPluginStart\n- Fix observeResponse docstring to match actual call sites (Get/Update)\n- Clone selector cache maps on set/get to prevent internal state mutation\n- Make Dispatcher.Stop() idempotent via CompareAndSwap\n- Clone Labels map on all MemoryStore return paths (Put, Delete,\n  DeleteByConnection, ScanByLabel, ScanByResourceKey)\n\n* fix(resource): third round of review fixes for PR #29\n\n- Replace separate Get+Put in observeResponse with atomic PutIfAbsent\n  to eliminate race with concurrent watch events\n- Populate Old field in indexer EventUpdate so dispatcher calls OnUpdate\n  instead of treating as Add\n- Include Label in edgeKey to prevent deduping edges with different labels\n- Extract cleanupPluginGraphState helper and call it on plugin restart\n  to clear stale registry entries, graph edges, and declarations\n- Add recover guard in dispatcher safeSend to handle the narrow race\n  where Stop() closes the events channel between select and send\n\n* fix(resource): inherit source namespace for fieldPath-extracted targets\n\nTarget nodes created by fieldPath extraction had Namespace hardcoded\nto \"\", causing key mismatches with real namespaced nodes (e.g.,\nReplicaSet in \"default\" namespace). Now defaults to the source entry''s\nnamespace, which is correct for ownership and intra-namespace refs.","tree":{"sha":"5c47898d84649d6bc332e25c61273dff7f3d1df6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/5c47898d84649d6bc332e25c61273dff7f3d1df6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/14e64a7c5a14227c5760417d0d3255ca78a616d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c47898d84649d6bc332e25c61273dff7f3d1df6\nparent 07b5ae8026d897d22162a13eae4ba7d43454e8cd\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1773627777 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773627777 -0500\n\nfeat(resource): add Resource Graph Engine (#29)\n\n* feat(resource): add ref-counted string interner for graph edge dedup\n\n* feat(resource): add ResourceEntry, RegistryStore interface, and MemoryStore implementation\n\n* feat(resource): add ResourceIndexer interface and async dispatcher\n\n* feat(resource): add RelationshipGraph with bidirectional edge management\n\nIntroduces GraphNode, GraphEdge, DependencyTree types and RelationshipGraph\nwith forward/reverse maps, dedup, selector cache, declaration registry, and\nconnection-scoped removal that preserves cross-connection edges.\n\n* feat(resource): add graph query APIs (GetRelated, GetRelationshipChain, GetDependencyTree)\n\n* feat(resource): add GraphIndexer for edge extraction from declarations\n\n* feat(resource): restructure sink to update registry/indexers unconditionally\n\n* feat(resource): wire registry, dispatcher, and graph into controller\n\n* feat(resource): add GraphService for Wails-bound graph queries\n\nIntroduces GraphService wrapping RelationshipGraph with GetRelated,\nGetRelationshipChain, and GetDependencyTree query methods. Adds Graph()\naccessor to Controller interface and concrete implementation.\n\n* test(resource): add end-to-end integration tests for registry→graph pipeline\n\n* fix(resource): address review findings from graph engine implementation\n\n- Populate Labels/UID/CreatedAt from watch metadata in sink entries\n  (fixes broken label-selector relationship resolution)\n- Prevent observeResponse from overwriting existing registry metadata\n- Return slice copies from EdgesFrom/EdgesTo to avoid data races\n- Add Dispatcher.Flush() barrier for deterministic test synchronization\n- Guard Dispatcher.Enqueue against sends after Stop\n- Improve RemoveEdgesForConnection comment clarity\n\n* chore: bump plugin-sdk to v0.3.1\n\n* fix(resource): address remaining review findings for PR #29\n\n- Fix TOCTOU race in dispatcher Enqueue/Flush with stopping channel\n- Clone labels maps in sink and memory store to prevent shared-map mutation\n- Use composite declMapKey for declarations to prevent cross-plugin overwrites\n- Validate direction input in GraphService instead of defaulting\n- Add cross-connection check in CheckLabelSelectorsForEntry\n- Add Shutdown method to controller for clean dispatcher teardown\n- Rename misleading interner test names\n- Document Key() separator invariant\n\n* fix(resource): second round of review fixes for PR #29\n\n- Add 30s timeout context for bootstrap RPCs in OnPluginStart\n- Fix observeResponse docstring to match actual call sites (Get/Update)\n- Clone selector cache maps on set/get to prevent internal state mutation\n- Make Dispatcher.Stop() idempotent via CompareAndSwap\n- Clone Labels map on all MemoryStore return paths (Put, Delete,\n  DeleteByConnection, ScanByLabel, ScanByResourceKey)\n\n* fix(resource): third round of review fixes for PR #29\n\n- Replace separate Get+Put in observeResponse with atomic PutIfAbsent\n  to eliminate race with concurrent watch events\n- Populate Old field in indexer EventUpdate so dispatcher calls OnUpdate\n  instead of treating as Add\n- Include Label in edgeKey to prevent deduping edges with different labels\n- Extract cleanupPluginGraphState helper and call it on plugin restart\n  to clear stale registry entries, graph edges, and declarations\n- Add recover guard in dispatcher safeSend to handle the narrow race\n  where Stop() closes the events channel between select and send\n\n* fix(resource): inherit source namespace for fieldPath-extracted targets\n\nTarget nodes created by fieldPath extraction had Namespace hardcoded\nto \"\", causing key mismatches with real namespaced nodes (e.g.,\nReplicaSet in \"default\" namespace). Now defaults to the source entry''s\nnamespace, which is correct for ownership and intra-namespace refs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt2mBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWHQQAHjzMCIyjmNUwDLRDVx1kotU\nLWq7Fh2NwXkdt/m7kUXQRh6bMAllII3F+lvNSuTteu6ARobceN/9hr4qV0EzsP8/\n/+OaGigs6QxcIWpm/PLaFc5CA/Y8ZEpKR7zTcLwg1km2xXfNjn7ujUhsZm8i37rl\nAaFruWmXV1lEdYu0d/AjV+v3vGCiFaX3DrDPNCBaCz8f2Wde2GNOMlEq4qTGCT37\nDo8oZUxS/hLxbJw8LWq4e3zq5+7w8rDSzucVbG8fRU1f+4GDaP8iB3HAWFAif6em\nqb5bW06HNzykBwc01Uek0F6daxvtt7bCGtHlHNZABa+06uogtD1xmg9Qy374Ri6P\nfWZjBNEBZNEvAtdjm0DlIaqN+eR2kZhOWPLnsidZlg4NaeznH8DIV6nXYhfeYJc2\nJdyA9TaOfZ5UQ55qVtbYMpCuzd8e//RL7u/7FhaRDL79mzQzzGRb5JPe71uvCv/o\n3A2trJ8BQxvTxt5RNudY0KeXc997xgCeoN4cHBo5ybg3Q3X3oQpnI6o8nrLgEl9j\nMGxS/LMSV302O0YFnc5zUzbZEBI45vcF9Oeybs6SyY11DdUXVPzhLtXY4ItE02Xs\nTNA4lk6hzjrDvulGkP+eg/WPVj6PH/SQqkvApbSK0CwFKAJIH5V3B0c94B8tqKlx\nOdxH8W3pVIyy5gMgjSe9\n=BK7y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-16T02:22:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com