bservability phase 2 — error recording, build-time config, SDK v0.3.0 (#28)\n\n* deps: add otelgrpc for gRPC client stats handler\n\n* feat: add noop metric and log exporter types for hot-toggle\n\n* feat: add switchable exporter wrappers for runtime signal toggling\n\n* feat: switchable exporters in Init(), add ApplyConfig() for hot-toggle\n\n* feat: inject telemetry env vars into plugin process commands\n\n* test: add ApplyConfig hot-toggle integration tests\n\n* feat: observability phase 2 — span error recording, build-time telemetry config, SDK v0.3.0\n\n- Add recordError(span, err) to all error paths across 6 controllers\n  for error visibility in Grafana traces\n- Remove long-lived spans from background listeners (Watch, Stream)\n  to prevent unbounded trace accumulation\n- Add per-event spans for meaningful operations in listeners\n- Fix ZapBackend to extract trace_id/span_id from OTel span context\n  instead of logging raw context object\n- Add build-time ldflags for telemetry secrets (OTLP endpoint, auth\n  header/value, Pyroscope endpoint) in release and nightly CI workflows\n- Production DefaultConfig now uses build-time vars so credentials\n  are injected at compile time, never in source\n- Bump plugin-sdk to v0.3.0 (OTel tracing, settings hot-toggle,\n  traceparent validation, atomic SetSettings)\n\n* fix: use separate Grafana user/token for build-time auth injection\n\nldflags values cannot contain spaces, so split the auth into\nbuildGrafanaUser (instance ID) and buildGrafanaToken (API key),\nthen construct \"Basic <base64>\" at runtime. Also adds Pyroscope\nBasicAuth support for Grafana Cloud Profiles.\n\n* fix: address review findings — security, context propagation, telemetry hardening\n\nSecurity:\n- Add path traversal validation in data controller (safe regex for keys/plugin IDs)\n- Add filepath.Clean + \"..\" containment check in fileloader\n- Remove auth credential injection into plugin process env vars\n- Remove build-time secret injection (Grafana user/token) from CI workflows\n- Redact terminal payload data from exec controller debug logs\n\nContext propagation:\n- Accept ctx in Reconcile, ReconcileFromFilesystem, CleanupStaleProcesses\n- Pass ctx through networker getConnectedCtx and exec getConnectedCtx\n- Use passed ctx instead of context.Background() in error logging paths\n\nTelemetry hardening:\n- Use WithEndpointURL instead of WithEndpoint+WithInsecure for OTLP exporters\n- Rollback meter provider to noop on otelruntime.Start failure\n- Log swap helper shutdown errors to stderr instead of discarding\n- Merge settings into existing config instead of replacing (telemetryFromSettings)\n- Add recordError on span for plugin-not-found in settings controller\n\nCode quality:\n- Extract cleanupPluginLocked helper in exec controller (deduplicate teardown)\n- Deferred recordError pattern with named returns in exec session methods\n- Persist ResetSetting changes via SaveSettings before notifying handlers\n\n* fix: review round 3 — path traversal, shared telemetryutil, RWMutex, staged SetSettings\n\n- Replace regex key validation with filepath containment checks (data controller, fileloader)\n- Extract shared telemetryutil.RecordError, remove 6 duplicate definitions\n- ApplyConfig accepts context.Context, uses passed ctx for exporter creation\n- Change telemetry Service mutex to RWMutex for Config() read access\n- SetSettings validates all settings before mutating state (stage-then-commit)\n- Deferred recordError on settings controller GetSetting/SetSetting/SetSettings\n- Dev mode config prefers build-time endpoints over localhost defaults\n- Redact devPath from info-level log, improve mergeAndWritePluginState error message\n\n* fix: review round 4 — staged ApplyConfig, nil guard, async handlers, log hygiene\n\n- ApplyConfig stages all exporters/profiler before swapping (no partial mutation)\n- Include AuthHeader/AuthValue/PyroscopeEndpoint changes in rebuild condition\n- RecordError guards against nil err to prevent panic\n- CheckConnection records getProvider error on span\n- Settings controller: descriptive log messages, redact settings values (log keys only)\n- Deferred recordError already captures gRPC errors via named returns\n- Marketplace URL log redacted to host only\n- notifyChangeHandlers dispatches handlers asynchronously\n- SetSettings rolls back in-memory state on SaveSettings failure\n- Logs controller goroutine uses span-linked context for trace correlation\n- Manager devPath removed from info-level log\n- MasterSwitchOff test verifies no spans exported after disable","tree":{"sha":"72fb8b736b36b1e7925d8775367632ac664b8dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/72fb8b736b36b1e7925d8775367632ac664b8dff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/07b5ae8026d897d22162a13eae4ba7d43454e8cd","verification":{"payload":"tree 72fb8b736b36b1e7925d8775367632ac664b8dff\nparent 9dd1bcbb1f2aa7a2a5b6b3579d47163591dce53e\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1773369463 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773369463 -0500\n\nfeat: observability phase 2 — error recording, build-time config, SDK v0.3.0 (#28)\n\n* deps: add otelgrpc for gRPC client stats handler\n\n* feat: add noop metric and log exporter types for hot-toggle\n\n* feat: add switchable exporter wrappers for runtime signal toggling\n\n* feat: switchable exporters in Init(), add ApplyConfig() for hot-toggle\n\n* feat: inject telemetry env vars into plugin process commands\n\n* test: add ApplyConfig hot-toggle integration tests\n\n* feat: observability phase 2 — span error recording, build-time telemetry config, SDK v0.3.0\n\n- Add recordError(span, err) to all error paths across 6 controllers\n  for error visibility in Grafana traces\n- Remove long-lived spans from background listeners (Watch, Stream)\n  to prevent unbounded trace accumulation\n- Add per-event spans for meaningful operations in listeners\n- Fix ZapBackend to extract trace_id/span_id from OTel span context\n  instead of logging raw context object\n- Add build-time ldflags for telemetry secrets (OTLP endpoint, auth\n  header/value, Pyroscope endpoint) in release and nightly CI workflows\n- Production DefaultConfig now uses build-time vars so credentials\n  are injected at compile time, never in source\n- Bump plugin-sdk to v0.3.0 (OTel tracing, settings hot-toggle,\n  traceparent validation, atomic SetSettings)\n\n* fix: use separate Grafana user/token for build-time auth injection\n\nldflags values cannot contain spaces, so split the auth into\nbuildGrafanaUser (instance ID) and buildGrafanaToken (API key),\nthen construct \"Basic <base64>\" at runtime. Also adds Pyroscope\nBasicAuth support for Grafana Cloud Profiles.\n\n* fix: address review findings — security, context propagation, telemetry hardening\n\nSecurity:\n- Add path traversal validation in data controller (safe regex for keys/plugin IDs)\n- Add filepath.Clean + \"..\" containment check in fileloader\n- Remove auth credential injection into plugin process env vars\n- Remove build-time secret injection (Grafana user/token) from CI workflows\n- Redact terminal payload data from exec controller debug logs\n\nContext propagation:\n- Accept ctx in Reconcile, ReconcileFromFilesystem, CleanupStaleProcesses\n- Pass ctx through networker getConnectedCtx and exec getConnectedCtx\n- Use passed ctx instead of context.Background() in error logging paths\n\nTelemetry hardening:\n- Use WithEndpointURL instead of WithEndpoint+WithInsecure for OTLP exporters\n- Rollback meter provider to noop on otelruntime.Start failure\n- Log swap helper shutdown errors to stderr instead of discarding\n- Merge settings into existing config instead of replacing (telemetryFromSettings)\n- Add recordError on span for plugin-not-found in settings controller\n\nCode quality:\n- Extract cleanupPluginLocked helper in exec controller (deduplicate teardown)\n- Deferred recordError pattern with named returns in exec session methods\n- Persist ResetSetting changes via SaveSettings before notifying handlers\n\n* fix: review round 3 — path traversal, shared telemetryutil, RWMutex, staged SetSettings\n\n- Replace regex key validation with filepath containment checks (data controller, fileloader)\n- Extract shared telemetryutil.RecordError, remove 6 duplicate definitions\n- ApplyConfig accepts context.Context, uses passed ctx for exporter creation\n- Change telemetry Service mutex to RWMutex for Config() read access\n- SetSettings validates all settings before mutating state (stage-then-commit)\n- Deferred recordError on settings controller GetSetting/SetSetting/SetSettings\n- Dev mode config prefers build-time endpoints over localhost defaults\n- Redact devPath from info-level log, improve mergeAndWritePluginState error message\n\n* fix: review round 4 — staged ApplyConfig, nil guard, async handlers, log hygiene\n\n- ApplyConfig stages all exporters/profiler before swapping (no partial mutation)\n- Include AuthHeader/AuthValue/PyroscopeEndpoint changes in rebuild condition\n- RecordError guards against nil err to prevent panic\n- CheckConnection records getProvider error on span\n- Settings controller: descriptive log messages, redact settings values (log keys only)\n- Deferred recordError already captures gRPC errors via named returns\n- Marketplace URL log redacted to host only\n- notifyChangeHandlers dispatches handlers asynchronously\n- SetSettings rolls back in-memory state on SaveSettings failure\n- Logs controller goroutine uses span-linked context for trace correlation\n- Manager devPath removed from info-level log\n- MasterSwitchOff test verifies no spans exported after disable","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJps3h3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkM8QAFX3QuHZTU/nykKzx1JH25N1\nQTXiBSvaK6m0bgJ4yUFF6d3bjCs2trns0aX6wI38vmZeYamwCLwtm+d/D5VltwXt\nChXJAWtwcxDHhg2uUxhPZtqqq2zmFLkjr/aR/hzHSlGBklDebgxwwIbrMBRaMGLP\n2LY0X9XbrtR