v plugins whose Vite server hasn''t started yet are deferred and loaded\nreactively when the plugin/devserver/status event fires with a ready\nstate, fixing the race where the UI import would fail or timeout because\nthe dev server wasn''t up yet.","tree":{"sha":"c6578cccf82cb4da8b1fc7bbabb55623934d9afb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/c6578cccf82cb4da8b1fc7bbabb55623934d9afb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/9dd1bcbb1f2aa7a2a5b6b3579d47163591dce53e","verification":{"payload":"tree c6578cccf82cb4da8b1fc7bbabb55623934d9afb\nparent 36646d4da72c5c95721f524e4d26e7b2cee3a151\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1773336526 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773336526 -0500\n\nfix: eliminate startup lag by parallelizing plugin loading and removing UI gate (#27)\n\nBackend: replace sequential plugin loading loop with a bounded concurrent\nworker pool (max 4 goroutines). With N plugins, startup now takes\nmax(t1..tN) instead of t1+t2+...+tN.\n\nFrontend: PluginServiceProvider no longer blocks the entire React tree\nuntil all plugins finish loading — children render immediately and the\nrouter builds incrementally as plugins become ready.\n\nDev plugins whose Vite server hasn''t started yet are deferred and loaded\nreactively when the plugin/devserver/status event fires with a ready\nstate, fixing the race where the UI import would fail or timeout because\nthe dev server wasn''t up yet.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpsvfOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuQwQAGMIQ1b4RpwIJ4Gu2PP/m3pS\nzYQHlfWkWufv3N7eepbjBwPykcrDIUpNGFSmuMe0MovTrPOWRQSBZJpemgrwRFSr\nJlZ3Lsy9N5UIvNXVcKL4fTN7bdruq7ymd45kFpAFp8T+ZSjNxWI5gy0Grlu79aB8\n13xrsFdRDaMdrpsA+eO3s2v9YjJ46kT2BgbtRf6QJdboD7HVoMzPiAjt0V78wL7o\nrDzabwKCsqB4H11yQYuCZjxKs3ybMCM6DNUqpnB74VhqK2J3jNO0BO6fSNuzmEor\nkOi39KE32+aldsGRSOvCqh2rVtmrpqsvmFl4i5clHXKvs+uZQ/ctplaslWG6fFYY\n05xE7OshLfd6PK64KFyHBQlEaOk