t coverage\n- Remove unused moduleHash from InstalledPluginDescriptor\n- Clarify README: routes API, extension point definition docs","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpsOyXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfGkQADm2iSPQ2ViAg07QqG7TrFoL\n/JchDfraPJ4owmHtx38ZnHB7OIMDsUwsF2X154MT3XZ9py7o4ce9e0qVERRq8J5r\nmN7soyCD8Vk60x4tSEDfVIvyN4Uus8++5jwQCavgRMswJILYDLslBRbwnFt7nCLc\noUr5E+4iJAyDq9p80DWroEmIQhRkZPuqybvxgUXCCI9pPxVdkFTxjlMuCakFq098\nHWgR81OZJc7fFJx9VfBZj+I9NmfMNGHDb3bad1eu/qY43CksLbnrD2JcqNVZ7X/U\niYeOfQgPANjRZcTOQwcGUoARaXVdDAnqowBPSpn6AArFgBDPwqYAk6s0jG33thzM\n5tb7W+rQIx5LAhlcjHh2kHySMKhbsldNAaZQYe7PIOsHcj6kMNsZ0cTcosjubPwY\nexFkEAPohvVB29hqg19xM2QN4fJ/fitqFyFSveTMjLQd4M4TDOzdy8RBAmPGloXS\nDBz5GSpxhjZ3rMwDV9lUT2mwG8hXJ6/3IPK2S9bpiSC4hZwzIyblx1h/ofZHZKA/\naUa0RfJUIExLbrJhZh2hQuJFIszgo6PdPNhym8WX9mLB+jaVeHTi7gGXbhnnpgbJ\nRNNbDAfPGouL3zSou4Dypc4FLwLi8xdp19ltVDY2dDPt9F7hRYAQQwCFtBycV9uB\nPNlrsO8jNjMWhx6TGaEq\n=hU1v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-11T04:16:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/fc1c4056fc4b716da95a5580e6a8837fd3557c5a","node_id":"C_kwDOLcPQu9oAKGZjMWM0MDU2ZmM0YjcxNmRhOTVhNTU4MGU2YTg4MzdmZDM1NTdjNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/omniviewdev/omniview/commit/c16bc274d694a641de0669e62a8b37932af9d27a","sha":"c16bc274d694a641de0669e62a8b37932af9d27a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/c16bc274d694a641de0669e62a8b37932af9d27a"}],"sha":"fc1c4056fc4b716da95a5580e6a8837fd3557c5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/fc1c4056fc4b716da95a5580e6a8837fd3557c5a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65102852?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joshuapare","id":65102852,"login":"joshuapare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTAyODUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshuapare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/commits/c16bc274d694a641de0669e62a8b37932af9d27a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-10T03:39:48Z","email":"65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Joshua Pare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-10T03:39:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: plugin concurrency, networker logging, and SDK v0.2.1 (#23)\n\n* fix: serialize concurrent plugin reloads and prevent double lifecycle calls\n\nTwo bugs caused a fatal \"concurrent map writes\" panic during dev-mode\nplugin reloads:\n\n1. When multiple Go files changed simultaneously, the per-file debounce\n   timers in goWatcherProcess fired separate handleRebuild calls that\n   both invoked ReloadPlugin concurrently for the same plugin. This\n   caused two goroutines to execute startPlugin simultaneously, racing\n   on controller map writes (clients, inChans, handlerMap, etc).\n\n   Fix: add a per-plugin operations mutex (pluginOpsLocks) that\n   serializes LoadPlugin, ReloadPlugin, and UnloadPlugin for the same\n   plugin ID. ReloadPlugin now holds the lock for the entire\n   unload→load cycle.\n\n2. stopPlugin and shutdownPlugin called the settings controller\n   explicitly, then iterated all detected capabilities without skipping\n   CapabilitySettings — potentially calling it twice. While\n   capStringsToCapabilities already filters settings from detected caps,\n   the guard was missing for cases where capabilities are stored on the\n   record directly (e.g. from plugin.yaml).\n\n   Fix: add CapabilitySettings skip in startPlugin, stopPlugin, and\n   shutdownPlugin capability loops, matching initPlugin''s existing\n   pattern.\n\nTests:\n- TestConcurrentReloads_Serialized: 10 concurrent ReloadPlugin calls\n  with race detector — verifies no panics or races\n- TestStartPlugin_SettingsNotCalledTwice: verifies settings controller\n  OnPluginStart is called exactly once\n- TestStopPlugin_SettingsNotCalledTwice: same for OnPluginStop\n- TestShutdownPlugin_SettingsNotCalledTwice: same for OnPluginShutdown\n\n* fix: add mutex protection to all plugin controller map accesses\n\nFive of seven plugin controllers had completely unprotected concurrent\nmap access, which could cause \"concurrent map writes\" panics when\nlifecycle methods (OnPluginStart/Stop) ran simultaneously with session\nor query operations.\n\nControllers fixed:\n- logs: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients, sessionIndex, inChans,\n  handlerMap\n- exec: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients, sessionIndex, inChans,\n  handlerMap, stops; also protects sessionIndex deletes in runMux and\n  runLocalMux goroutines\n- settings: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients\n- networker: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients, sessionIndex, stops\n- metric: extended existing mux to also protect clients and inChans\n  (previously only covered providerInfos, handlerMap, resourceIndex)\n\nThe resource controller was already properly protected with\nsync.RWMutex and did not need changes.\n\nPattern applied consistently:\n- Lock() for all map writes (OnPluginStart, OnPluginStop, session\n  create/close, goroutine session cleanup)\n- RLock() for all map reads (ListPlugins, HasPlugin, session lookups,\n  client dispatch)\n- RPC calls (Dispense, GetSupportedResources) happen outside the lock\n  to avoid holding it during network I/O\n\nTests:\n- TestController_ConcurrentMapAccess: 40 goroutines doing concurrent\n  read/write/delete on controller maps with race detector\n- TestController_ConcurrentSessionIndex: concurrent sessionIndex\n  read/write/delete with race detector\n- Full test suite passes with -race across all plugin packages\n\n* feat: add networker port-forward logging and CheckConnection support\n\n- Add structured logging throughout the networker controller''s\n  StartResourcePortForwardingSession and getConnectedCtx paths\n- Return explicit error when getConnectedCtx fails instead of passing\n  nil plugin context to the plugin\n- Add CheckConnection RPC support to the resource controller, adapter,\n  client, provider, and service layers\n- Regenerate Wails bindings\n\n* fix: UI tweaks for connection table, resource view, and homepage card\n\n* chore: bump plugin-sdk to v0.2.1\n\n* chore: migrate golangci-lint configs to v2 format\n\n- Add version: \"2\" and restructure all config files for golangci-lint v2\n- Rename gomnd → mnd, move gci/goimports to formatters section\n- Remove deprecated linters (exportloopref, execinquery, tenv, typecheck, etc.)\n- Fix stale infraview import prefixes → omniviewdev\n- Remove plugins/aws/.golangci.yml (plugin will move to its own repo)\n\n* fix: address PR review findings — races, stale state, sanitization, and UI fixes\n\nBackend:\n- Return defensive copies from exec GetPluginHandlers/GetHandlers to prevent\n  callers from mutating internal maps outside the mutex\n- Capture and log errors from concurrent ReloadPlugin calls in test\n- Clean up logs controller handlerMap on plugin stop/shutdown to prevent\n  stale handlers from being advertised\n- Fix send-on-closed-channel race in logs SendCommand and metric Unsubscribe\n  by holding the mutex during the channel send\n- Sanitize crash context log entries to redact tokens, secrets, and long\n  hex/base64 strings before persisting or emitting to frontend\n- Wrap CheckConnection errors through toAppError and checkConnectionError\n  for consistency with other Wails-bound RPCs\n\nFrontend:\n- Use index-based React key for suggestion list items to avoid duplicate keys\n- Memoize PluginContext.Provider value in HomepageCard to prevent unnecessary\n  re-renders\n- Use isNaN(getTime()) instead of string comparison for invalid date check\n- Type ScanOptions.scanners as Scanner[] instead of string[]\n\n* fix: enable missing linters, fix exec controller races and cleanup, reorder error check\n\n- Add exhaustruct and gomodguard to golangci-lint enable lists (settings existed but linters weren''t enabled)\n- Add goimports local-prefixes to match gci prefix configuration\n- Fix exec runMux using sessionID as channel key instead of pluginID via sessionIndex\n- Hold RLock during channel sends in exec controller to prevent send-on-closed-channel panics\n- Clean up exec handlerMap in OnPluginStop/OnPluginShutdown to prevent stale resource handlers\n- Move groups.isError check above !groups.data early return so errors render properly\n\n* fix: remove dead config, unused field, and consolidate exec controller locking\n\n- Remove dead wrapcheck exclusion from both golangci configs (linter not enabled)\n- Remove unused stops map field from exec controller\n- Avoid holding RLock during blocking channel sends in runMux and WriteSession\n- Add safeSend helper with recover guard for closed-channel safety\n- Consolidate double-RLock pattern in session methods via lookupSession helper\n- Clean up exec handlerMap in OnPluginStop/OnPluginShutdown\n\n* fix: exec controller — surface safeSend errors, complete shutdown cleanup, defer registration until stream succeeds\n\n- safeSend now returns error so WriteSession propagates failures to callers\n- OnPluginShutdown cleans up inChans and sessionIndex to prevent stale blocked writes\n- OnPluginStart calls provider.Stream before registering state to avoid leaked channels on stream failure\n\n* fix: use named return in safeSend and purge sessionIndex in OnPluginStop\n\n- Use named return (err error) so deferred recover properly propagates\n  the error to callers instead of returning nil on panic\n- Purge stale sessionIndex entries in OnPluginStop matching the stopped\n  pluginID, consistent with OnPluginShutdown cleanup","tree":{"sha":"77c03fc519880619008d480faefdb42eb5045ac9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/trees/77c03fc519880619008d480faefdb42eb5045ac9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omniviewdev/omniview/git/commits/c16bc274d694a641de0669e62a8b37932af9d27a","verification":{"payload":"tree 77c03fc519880619008d480faefdb42eb5045ac9\nparent 4917c91b0ede70d40ec7c690022d148c7a4ad2ea\nauthor Joshua Pare <65102852+joshuapare@users.noreply.github.com> 1773113988 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773113988 -0500\n\nfix: plugin concurrency, networker logging, and SDK v0.2.1 (#23)\n\n* fix: serialize concurrent plugin reloads and prevent double lifecycle calls\n\nTwo bugs caused a fatal \"concurrent map writes\" panic during dev-mode\nplugin reloads:\n\n1. When multiple Go files changed simultaneously, the per-file debounce\n   timers in goWatcherProcess fired separate handleRebuild calls that\n   both invoked ReloadPlugin concurrently for the same plugin. This\n   caused two goroutines to execute startPlugin simultaneously, racing\n   on controller map writes (clients, inChans, handlerMap, etc).\n\n   Fix: add a per-plugin operations mutex (pluginOpsLocks) that\n   serializes LoadPlugin, ReloadPlugin, and UnloadPlugin for the same\n   plugin ID. ReloadPlugin now holds the lock for the entire\n   unload→load cycle.\n\n2. stopPlugin and shutdownPlugin called the settings controller\n   explicitly, then iterated all detected capabilities without skipping\n   CapabilitySettings — potentially calling it twice. While\n   capStringsToCapabilities already filters settings from detected caps,\n   the guard was missing for cases where capabilities are stored on the\n   record directly (e.g. from plugin.yaml).\n\n   Fix: add CapabilitySettings skip in startPlugin, stopPlugin, and\n   shutdownPlugin capability loops, matching initPlugin''s existing\n   pattern.\n\nTests:\n- TestConcurrentReloads_Serialized: 10 concurrent ReloadPlugin calls\n  with race detector — verifies no panics or races\n- TestStartPlugin_SettingsNotCalledTwice: verifies settings controller\n  OnPluginStart is called exactly once\n- TestStopPlugin_SettingsNotCalledTwice: same for OnPluginStop\n- TestShutdownPlugin_SettingsNotCalledTwice: same for OnPluginShutdown\n\n* fix: add mutex protection to all plugin controller map accesses\n\nFive of seven plugin controllers had completely unprotected concurrent\nmap access, which could cause \"concurrent map writes\" panics when\nlifecycle methods (OnPluginStart/Stop) ran simultaneously with session\nor query operations.\n\nControllers fixed:\n- logs: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients, sessionIndex, inChans,\n  handlerMap\n- exec: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients, sessionIndex, inChans,\n  handlerMap, stops; also protects sessionIndex deletes in runMux and\n  runLocalMux goroutines\n- settings: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients\n- networker: added sync.RWMutex protecting clients, sessionIndex, stops\n- metric: extended existing mux to also protect clients and inChans\n  (previously only covered providerInfos, handlerMap, resourceIndex)\n\nThe resource controller was already properly protected with\nsync.RWMutex and did not need changes.\n\nPattern applied consistently:\n- Lock() for all map writes (OnPluginStart, OnPluginStop, session\n  create/close, goroutine session cleanup)\n- RLock() for all map reads (ListPlugins, HasPlugin, session lookups,\n  client dispatch)\n- RPC calls (Dispense, GetSupportedResources) happen outside the lock\n  to avoid holding it during network I/O\n\nTests:\n- TestController_ConcurrentMapAccess: 40 goroutines doing concurrent\n  read/write/delete on controller maps with race detector\n- TestController_ConcurrentSessionIndex: concurrent sessionIndex\n  read/write/delete with race detector\n- Full test suite passes with -race across all plugin packages\n\n* feat: add networker port-forward logging and CheckConnection support\n\n- Add structured logging throughout the networker controller''s\n  StartResourcePortForwardingSession and getConnectedCtx paths\n- Return explicit error when getConnectedCtx fails instead of passing\n  nil plugin context to the plugin\n- Add CheckConnection RPC support to the resource controller, adapter,\n  client, provider, and service layers\n- Regenerate Wails bindings\n\n* fix: UI tweaks for connection table, resource view, and homepage card\n\n* chore: bump plugin-sdk to v0.2.1\n\n* chore: migrate golangci-lint configs to v2 format\n\n- Add version: \"2\" and restructure all config files for golangci-lint v2\n- Rename gomnd → mnd, move gci/goimports to formatters section\n- Remove deprecated linters (exportloopref, execinquery, tenv, typecheck, etc.)\n- Fix stale infraview import prefixes → omniviewdev\n- Remove plugins/aws/.golangci.yml (plugin will move to its own repo)\n\n* fix: address PR review findings — races, stale state, sanitization, and UI fixes\n\nBackend:\n- Return defensive copies from exec GetPluginHandlers/GetHandlers to prevent\n  callers from mutating internal maps outside the mutex\n- Capture and log errors from concurrent ReloadPlugin calls in test\n- Clean up logs controller handlerMap on plugin stop/shutdown to prevent\n  stale handlers from being advertised\n- Fix send-on-closed-channel race in logs SendCommand and metric Unsubscribe\n  by holding the mutex during the channel send\n- Sanitize crash context log entries to redact tokens, secrets, and long\n  hex/base64 strings before persisting or emitting to frontend\n- Wrap CheckConnection errors through toAppError and checkConnectionError\n  for consistency with other Wails-bound RPCs\n\nFrontend:\n- Use index-based React key for suggestion list items to avoid duplicate keys\n- Memoize PluginContext.Provider value in HomepageCard to prevent unnecessary\n  re-renders\n- Use isNaN(getTime()) instead of string comparison for invalid date check\n- Type ScanOptions.scanners as Scanner[] instead of string[]\n\n* fix: enable missing linters, fix exec controller races and cleanup, reorder error check\n\n- Add exhaustruct and gomodguard to golangci-lint enable lists (settings existed but linters weren''t enabled)\n- Add goimports local-prefixes to match gci prefix configuration\n- Fix exec runMux using sessionID as channel key instead of pluginID via sessionIndex\n- Hold RLock during channel sends in exec controller to prevent send-on-closed-channel panics\n- Clean up exec handlerMap in OnPluginStop/OnPluginShutdown to prevent stale resource handlers\n- Move groups.isError check above !groups.data early return so errors render properly\n\n* fix: remove dead config, unused field, and consolidate exec controller locking\n\n- Remove dead wrapcheck exclusion from both golangci configs (linter not enabled)\n- Remove unused stops map field from exec controller\n- Avoid holding RLock during blocking channel sends in runMux and WriteSession\n- Add safeSend helper with recover guard for closed-channel safety\n- Consolidate double-RLock pattern in session methods via lookupSession helper\n- Clean up exec handlerMap in OnPluginStop/OnPluginShutdown\n\n* fix: exec controller — surface safeSend errors, complete shutdown cleanup, defer registration until stream succeeds\n\n- safeSend now returns error so WriteSession propagates failures to callers\n- OnPluginShutdown cleans up inChans and sessionIndex to prevent stale blocked writes\n- OnPluginStart calls provider.Stream before registering state to avoid leaked channels on stream failure\n\n* fix: use named return in safeSend and purge sessionIndex in OnPluginStop\n\n- Use named return (err error) so deferred recover properly propagates\n  the error to callers instead of returning nil on panic\n- Purge stale sessionIndex entries in OnPluginStop matching the stopped\n  pluginID, consistent with OnPluginShutdown cleanup","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpr5KECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3ecQAEAxEWzCVDX1smW/jWaaOS+k\nE67ic5X0zbNXHRFrJaXmq07nXnY2TShop07e4jegOOSWUP+0xyiKOmu6Cbz02kF7\nvxajMScl9MjuTnkP9fimzD3WQckambxDMQEcBAP5pjVAI+60aAdmGBKNL6BTJ/Nn\nL1z2qAwx9K8rbr0n3JCWgPf5IZQpRn+vJ3FzaT1vs1bbPGonb2iVDTy9Y0PkywMi\nfUziUSrCeyxCv5RYCzbIR39G3r+d8Am8FX1KaHT1D6IxvKgje0XAhIvOC5v/0WaV\n3/jRj7cAnAnI+JmiI07feh2yvvCJzG4HGYPlPrJZdyXLOd/hj71EhWmV9AWu5w/N\n9POI9FVffj18AL32fV86RKQX0DsMOrnc+qgmeYtnuaQ9jSkPi53qN0xXpg2LSehj\nZKT/KquU1iwz3MZ+bFsv2Izbq8vCjmHOEUnSaqgS37VxYLvIJjfc8GZiliwQSUxA\nUqHBqIW6HI7xRL1owwFai7r6aIVR2VzjG5hXI3itXjEUQHc/T0hlmihMf9MHIRwN\nFgheoCKOwLPO7L1M+2T8Dq+y5/bWbvmNW6efT/GbB72PfEYj2JWIvXrm7pOlbQ46\nBieU049biuL/YJd7pjAup/3cPAiOSbMfzj3f/NkH3g1ej+DP/zHc535ZyCZQKHw9\njGOjJ7HrVe5EMAFxJXYX\n=Vbbz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-0